# IndangGO environment settings: every one the code reads, and the outside
# services behind them. This file is committed, so it holds placeholders only.
#
# Where real values go (all gitignored except this file):
#   .env           the app (Expo). Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* names reach the app, and
#                  they are built into it, so never put a secret here.
#   .env.backend   the API server (server.js loads it). Secrets live here.
#   Render         the deployed API and God view (render.yaml; secrets are set
#                  in the Render dashboard, marked `sync: false` there).
#   eas.json       EAS builds. EAS does not upload .env, so app settings for
#                  a cloud build go in that profile's `env`.
#
# Outside services and accounts:
#   MongoDB Atlas    database (users, sessions, rides, ratings, email codes).
#                    cloud.mongodb.com, free M0 cluster, Singapore region.
#   Brevo            sends sign-up and password reset codes by email.
#                    brevo.com, free 300 emails a day, HTTPS API.
#   Render           hosts the API (indanggo-api) and the God view website
#                    (indanggo-god-view). render.com, free tier.
#   Expo / EAS       development and release builds of the app (project
#                    owner and ID are in app.json). expo.dev.
#   GitHub           the code, and what Render deploys from.
#   OpenFreeMap      map tiles. No account or key.
#   OpenStreetMap    road and place data, bundled in assets/ (built with the
#                    Overpass API by scripts/build-road-graph.js). No key.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- .env (app)

# The API server. Optional in development (the app uses the PC running Metro,
# port 3000); required for a preview or release build, which has no Metro.
# Your PC on the Wi-Fi network, or the deployed API:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://indang-trike-app.onrender.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.100:3000

# TESTING ONLY. true makes a GPS fix outside Indang count as CvSU Main Campus,
# so passengers and drivers can book and take trips from anywhere. Development
# builds only: a release build ignores it (utils/testLocation.js).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TEST_ANYWHERE=true

# --------------------------------------------------- .env.backend (API server)

# MongoDB connection string. Atlas: Connect -> Drivers, with the database name
# before the "?". Without it the server uses a local MongoDB (start.bat/start.sh
# start one in Docker).
# MONGO_URL=mongodb+srv://USER:PASSWORD@CLUSTER.mongodb.net/indang_trike_db?retryWrites=true&w=majority
# MONGO_URL=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/indang_trike_db

# Port the API listens on (Render sets this itself).
# PORT=3000

# Which website may call the API from a browser (the God view). Default: any.
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://indanggo-god-view.onrender.com

# Brevo, for the emailed codes. The API key is under SMTP & API -> API keys;
# the sender must be verified under Senders, domains & dedicated IPs. Without
# the key and sender, sign-up and password reset answer "Email verification is
# not set up on this server".
# BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-...
# BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=you@gmail.com
# BREVO_SENDER_NAME=IndangGO

# God view admins log in with their existing app phone and password.
# Comma-separated approved numbers; empty turns admin access off.
# GOD_VIEW_ADMIN_PHONES=09171234567

# ------------------------------------------- God view website build (Render)

# The API the God view website calls; build.mjs writes it into the site.
# Must be https://. Set in render.yaml.
# GOD_VIEW_API_URL=https://indang-trike-app.onrender.com

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- tests

# npm run test:backend and test:god-view create a uniquely named database here
# and drop it afterwards. Give the server address without a database name or
# "?..." options. Atlas works too.
# TEST_MONGO_URL=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
